## 3. What riffcat actually contributed

### 3.1 Where riffcat's own engine did the work

A **facet** is riffcat's rule for which details a comparison ignores, such as constants, types or memory
offsets. **Content addressing** means code with the same shape under a facet gets the same hash, so copies
group together automatically.

| Finding | Mechanism |
|---|---|
| Sharing repeated code saves only about 8 to 10 KB after call costs | the run census under three facets (exact, memory offsets ignored, all constants ignored), keyed by core facet digests |
| Code that differs only in struct layout adds 4,424 bytes of repeats | the new memory-offset field class, erased by a view directive (no new dimension) |
| Different stack scheduling hides almost no repeats (603 bytes) | `evm-dataflow/1`: each block is lifted into a dataflow graph so DUP, SWAP and POP disappear |
| Ignoring types finds nothing beyond exact matches; 1,330 bytes are identical functions left unmerged | Sonatina IR function facets |
| `decode_from_bounded`'s 7 instances differ in structure, so one generic decoder would need runtime layout descriptors | the same facets, which showed that no facet merges them |
| The 161-byte prologue in five dispatcher arms is one construct: `env` passed by value | traced chains are content addressed, so the five group into one class |
| Fe and solc share no basic block of 16 bytes or more | cross-compiler matching (a null result) |

**Pattern:** the engine answered "is X the cause?" questions quickly and decisively, and mostly the answer
was no. That is valuable, because each no removed a line of work, such as an outlining pass or a type-erasure
design. It did not point at the causes that turned out to matter.

### 3.2 Where riffcat was bookkeeping

These joins could have been scripts. In riffcat they became replayable commands with conservation checks
that refuse to report when totals don't match the artifact.

- **The byte-origin ledger** (`bytes.rs`) joins Fe's per-instruction attribution to every byte.
- **"The port's own code is at parity with solc"** came from solc source-map attribution plus pairing by
  name (`sourcemap.rs`, `compare_functions.rs`). This was the most important single finding.
- **The stage view** (`stages.rs`, `fe_stages.rs`) walks Fe's origin edges from bytes back through Sonatina
  IR and MIR to source lines. It produced three findings:
  - the memory-op split;
  - the clamp's 115 call sites;
  - every `decode_from_bounded` call site tracing to `abi.fe:382`.
- **The excess ledger** (`byte_causes.rs`) places every byte of both runtimes in exactly one bucket, so the
  per-bucket differences add up to exactly the 40,088-byte gap.

### 3.3 What was not riffcat

- **The foundation:** Fe's `fe dev trace emit` and `fe dev debug emit --attribution-details`, which link
  each EVM instruction to its sources. riffcat depends on this; it cannot produce it.
- **Spill identification:** a probe that patched Sonatina to dump its memory plan.
- **The first "20% shuffles, six times the memory ops" comparison:** a 40-line opcode count. riffcat
  confirmed it later.
- **All contract sizes and Sonatina variant numbers:** builds and small Python scripts.
- **Code locations in Fe and Sonatina:** read directly.
- **The independent checks:** Python, on purpose.

